; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Petal Mandala
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     symmetry, petals, FILLED, REPEAT, rings, color
; SUMMARY:  Draws a mandala of three rings of painted petals, each ring turned to fit between the last.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A petal is made of two curved lines that meet at both ends. The
;   program paints rings of petals around the middle: 8 small ones,
;   then 12, then 24. Between the rings it adds circles of dots, and
;   a golden center finishes the flower.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the numbers of petals or the colors in the
;   calls at the bottom.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * making a curve from many small FORWARD and RIGHT steps
;   * the petal: two 90 degree curves with a 90 degree turn between
;   * placing shapes evenly around a circle: 360 / count
;   * offsetting a ring by half a step so petals fall in the gaps
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use 6, 12 and 18 petals for a calmer flower.
;   * Make the petals fatter with 120 degree curves (repeat 24).
;   * Pick your own color pairs for each ring.
; ============================================================

; PETAL paints one petal :len long, pointing the way the turtle
; faces, and leaves the turtle where it started.
to petal :len :color
  ; 18 steps of 5 degrees make a quarter circle. Its chord is the
  ; petal length, so each step is len / 18 times about 1.11.
  localmake "step :len * 1.11 / 18
  left 45
  filled :color [
    repeat 2 [
      repeat 18 [forward :step right 5]
      right 90
    ]
  ]
  right 45
end

; PETAL.RING puts :count petals around the middle, starting :inner
; steps out, each :len long, in two alternating colors.
to petal.ring :count :inner :len :colors :offset
  ; a thin cream outline around every petal
  setpencolor [250 240 230]
  setpensize 1.5
  for [k 1 :count] [
    penup home
    setheading :offset + :k * 360 / :count
    forward :inner
    pendown
    petal :len item 1 + remainder :k 2 :colors
  ]
end

; DOT.RING puts :count dots on a circle of radius :r.
to dot.ring :count :r :size :color
  setpencolor :color
  setpensize :size
  for [k 1 :count] [
    penup home setheading :k * 360 / :count forward :r
    dot pos
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [30 20 45]
petal.ring 8 25 70 [[230 80 120] [250 150 90]] 0
dot.ring 16 105 6 [250 220 120]
petal.ring 12 115 75 [[90 160 230] [140 110 220]] 15
dot.ring 24 200 7 [250 220 120]
petal.ring 24 210 70 [[80 200 160] [60 150 200]] 7.5
; the golden center
setpencolor [250 200 80] setpensize 36 dot [0 0]
setpencolor [255 240 170] setpensize 14 dot [0 0]
